# The criteria of an FFI program's Moore machine state, one step at a time: a state is a pair whose left field is in
# the computation graph's schema, and each next state is filtered again. A criterion is told by the identity of its
# interned term; the fixed point and Ω are written out in it.
#
# Ω stands at the positions a criterion leaves open, since Ω ∥ M ≃_O M (Lean: omegaParallelContextualEquivalence): a
# state's transition, a finish's answer, a method's or a constructor's symbols and a decoded value, whose type the
# descriptor at its position gives, a method's descriptor holding its value types.
λ export
. (λtuple. tuple λmixin. mixin mixin)
λ omega
. omega (omega (omega (omega corpora "library") "prelude") "list_cbor")
λ list_from_cbor _ _ _
. omega (omega (omega (omega corpora "library") "text") "cbor")
λ text_from_cbor _ _ _
. omega (omega (omega corpora "library") "top")
λ top
. omega (omega (omega (omega corpora "library") "java_ffi") "literals")
λ bits_8_list_type _ _ _ _
# bottom:
# Ω, the least term of ⊑_O.
. (λtuple. tuple λ. (λx. x x) λx. x x)
λ bottom
# expression_types:
# The expressions of a computation graph and their argument lists, one fixed point of their pair, so that each names
# the other as the same term, the pair's field: an expression is a call, a new, or a decode, a call's and a new's
# arguments the pair's lists; a list of arguments is a cons of an expression and the pair's lists, or nil.
. ( λtuple
    . tuple
      ( (λx f. f λ. x x f)
        (λx f. f λ. x x f)
        ( λ types s
          . s
            ( (λc n d. c ((λx. x x) λx. x x) (types λ_ a. a))
            + (λc n d. n ((λx. x x) λx. x x) ((λx. x x) λx. x x) (types λ_ a. a))
            + λc n d. d ((λx. x x) λx. x x)
            )
            ((λh t _ k. k h t) (types λe _. e) (types λ_ a. a) + λn _. n)
        )
      )
  )
λ expression_types
# expression_type:
# The expressions: the first of expression_types.
. (λtuple. tuple λon_call on_new on_decode. expression_types (λe _. e) on_call on_new on_decode)
λ expression_type
# arguments_type:
# The Scott lists (prelude/list) of expressions: the second of expression_types.
. (λtuple. tuple λon_nil on_cons. expression_types (λ_ a. a) on_nil on_cons)
λ arguments_type
# output_alphabet:
# The outputs: an answer, open, or an expression.
. ( λ tuple
    . tuple
    λ on_finish on_run
    . ((λf r. f ((λx. x x) λx. x x)) + λf r. r expression_type) on_finish on_run
  )
λ output_alphabet
# moore_state_type:
# The pairs of an output of the alphabet and a transition, open: one step of the machine.
. (λtuple. tuple λk. k output_alphabet ((λx. x x) λx. x x))
λ moore_state_type
# symbols:
# The symbols of a method, its owner, name and descriptor, each a list of UTF-8 bytes.
. (λtuple. tuple λowner name descriptor s. s owner name descriptor)
λ symbols
# symbols_type:
# The criterion of symbols.
. (λtuple. tuple λs. s bits_8_list_type bits_8_list_type bits_8_list_type)
λ symbols_type
# method_symbols:
# The symbols a method's CBOR array literal spells, λk. k ["owner", "name", "descriptor"], read in the term: the host
# reads no bit of a literal. A literal that is no array of three text strings has no symbols.
. ( λ tuple
    . tuple
    λ method
    . method
    λ
    . list_from_cbor text_from_cbor
    λ read
    . read top
    λ owner after_owner
    . after_owner top
    λ name after_name
    . after_name top
    λ descriptor after_descriptor
    . after_descriptor (symbols owner name descriptor) λ_ _. top
  )
λ method_symbols
. export bottom expression_type arguments_type output_alphabet moore_state_type symbols symbols_type method_symbols
